      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scipio%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Scipio originated in the late nineteenth century within Tobucksy County of the Choctaw Nation in the Indian Territory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/scipio_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office first opened at Scipio, Indian Territory, on January 24, 1890.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scipio%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Remnants of historical mills near the water's edge show how early settlers used Scipio Creek for grain processing.",
